<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dromichaetes</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 300 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dromichaetes was a king of the Getae north of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> around 300 BCE. In about 292 BCE he defeated and captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lysimachus">Lysimachus</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>, who had invaded his land. According to ancient writers he entertained his prisoner with a contrast between a plain Getic meal and a royal feast, then released him in return for the restoration of lands and a marriage alliance.</p></div>
